      "title": "Estella ->  Villamayor de Monjardin  ",
  "distance": "11,2 km",
  "time": "4 hours 3 min",
  "short_desc": "Wine Fountains and a Cozy Family Stay.",
  "long_desc": "We started around 9 a.m. from Estella, a charming town with about 28,000 residents. Since we were only walking about 10 kilometers today, we allowed ourselves a later start. The morning was cool, but the temperature kept rising as the day went on. After about 4 kilometers, we reached Bodega Irache, a massive winery famous for its wine fountain, where pilgrims can help themselves to red wine from a tap. Suddenly, Lydia, an American woman from California, said, I’ll take the white wine! She thought the second tap offered white wine,  but it was just water! After a warm uphill stretch, we arrived in Villamayor de Monjardín, where we stayed with Betty and Bert and their two daughters. The family is originally from the Netherlands and has been running their bed and breakfast for two years. They only rent out three rooms, and the house, though old, is wonderfully charming and well-kept. The garden has a lovely, peaceful atmosphere. In the evening, we shared a pilgrim dinner with the family, delicious food and great company. Truly a great place to stay.",
