    {
      "week": 2,
      "day": 9,
      "title": "Villamayor de Monjardin -> Tores de Rio",
  "distance": "20,3 km",
  "time": "5 hours 5 min",
  "short_desc": "Routine, Rhythm and a Refreshing Dip in the pool.",
  "long_desc": "After 9 days on the Camino, life as a pilgrim is starting to settle into a natural rhythm. Wake-up at 6:30 a.m., breakfast at 7:00 a.m.and start walking by 8:00 a.m. Continuing until early afternoon, usually around 1 or 2 p.m. The rest of the day is reserved for rest and sightseeing, leading up to the traditional pilgrim dinner at 7 p.m. The body now follows the trail almost instinctively, with ease and without resistance. Today’s walk to Torres del Río was especially enjoyable. A perfect mix of clouds and sunshine, comfortable temperatures where Navarra showing off its best side. Rolling Basque farmlands and peaceful path made for a calm and satisfying walk. Along the way, we also ran into Cornelia from Casa Rural Montedeio, another familiar face on the Camino. We arrived at Hostel Rural San Andrés shortly after 1 p.m., grabbed a quick bite and then came the highlight of the day, a refreshing dip in the pool. Simple, deserved, and utterly rejuvenating. A perfect end to a day before the Pilgrims dinner. - - Hang tight. Pictures are on the way! Dealing with a slow internet connection.  .",
